# Progressive loading

**Canonical:** [`dashboard/page.tsx`](apps/frontend/src/app/[locale]/(app)/dashboard/page.tsx) + [`dashboard-skeletons.tsx`](apps/frontend/src/features/dashboard/dashboard-skeletons.tsx).  
**Full guide:** [`docs/frontend/progressive-loading.md`](docs/frontend/progressive-loading.md).

## Law

```text
1 independent data source = 1 Suspense = 1 UI-faithful section skeleton
```

Data dependency decides the boundary — not visual grouping.

## Must

1. Loading starts **inside** `<main>` only. Never skeleton Sidebar / Header / AppShellFrame.
2. Static UI (titles, icons, SubNav, CTAs, i18n labels) renders **immediately** — outside Suspense.
3. Each independent server fetch / async RSC section gets its **own** Suspense + matching skeleton.
4. Skeleton mirrors real UI (padding, grids, metric footer rail, table, filters). Use `.zarva-shimmer` (gold wash).
5. Shared API → `React.cache` → **one** Suspense (boxes may resolve together). Do not invent endpoints to fake independence.
6. **No** `(app)/loading.tsx` and **no** route `loading.tsx` when the page has section Suspense (double flash).
7. **Search / FilterSearch skeleton = full width** — same as live `FilterSearch` (`w-full`). Never `max-w-md` (or any narrower cap) on the loading search shell; width must not jump when Suspense resolves.

## Must not

- One Suspense / page-level `await` / `Promise.all` around unrelated fetches
- Generic full-page skeleton
- Skeletonizing static titles/icons from i18n
- Blank `<main>` while data loads
- Narrow search skeleton (`max-w-md` / fixed small width) that expands after load

## Checklist

1. List fetches → group shared vs independent
2. One Suspense + skeleton per independent source
3. Static chrome outside
4. No route `loading.tsx` ahead of section skeletons
5. RTL + responsive parity with loaded UI

## Patterns

| Kind | Do |
|------|-----|
| Dashboard-like hubs | Copy dashboard: page wires Suspense; feature `*-skeletons.tsx` |
| Domain lists | `StreamedDomainChrome` + body Suspense + `DomainListBodySkeleton` (+ real `skeletonKpiLabels`) |
| Section loaders / hubs | Chrome outside Suspense; body `DomainBodySkeleton` (`list`/`form`/`hub`); island `chrome="body"` |
| Detail / form | Chrome/SubNav outside; `showHeader={false}` when title is data-dependent; form body skeleton |
| Client Query only | Pending UI inside the page — not segment `loading.tsx` |
